cosmic-ext-ime (0.2.1+chewing) noble; urgency=medium

  * Add the Chewing (新酷音) Zhuyin engine on libchewing 0.6 with
    ibus-chewing 2.0 behaviour: on-demand candidate window with selection
    keys, paging and highlight navigation, editing keys, Ctrl+number user
    phrases and symbol lists, keypad handling, easy symbols, full-width
    punctuation, Caps Lock Chinese/English sub-mode, keyboard layouts
    (standard, Hsu, IBM, Gin-Yieh, ETen, ETen 26, Dvorak, DaChen 26);
    reuses an existing ibus-chewing user dictionary
  * Plain Zhuyin (傳統注音) option: every syllable opens the candidate
    list and a number key commits that character, no phrase conversion
  * Candidate window: optional horizontal (one-row) layout
  * Settings: Chewing section (keyboard, candidates per page, selection
    keys, space selection, auto-learn, symbols, cursor and phrase options)
  * Frontend: share the seat keymap with the virtual keyboard so
    cosmic-comp no longer rebuilds its xkb state on every forwarded key
    (input source and Caps Lock were lost mid-typing); drop the modifiers
    echo; follow input sources from settled layout reports (TLA+-verified
    policy); Caps Lock is a pure Chinese/English toggle while Chinese
    input is on and the Chinese source always starts in Chinese mode
  * Unit-tested frontend policies (key translation, dispatch, Shift tap,
    layout) and headless compositor probe tools under tools/

 -- Alan <alan@alanyho.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 23:20:00 -0800

